v 3
d 'LSMLM': Lee-Strazicich minimum LM unit root test with structural breaks
d
d lsmlm performs the Lee-Strazicich minimum LM unit root test with zero, one,
d or two endogenous structural breaks. Two deterministic models are available:
d crash (level shift) and break (level and trend shift). breaks(0) gives the
d Schmidt-Phillips no-break LM test. Critical values are interpolated over the
d sample size and, for the trend-break model, over the break fraction(s). The
d command runs on any tsset series and can be restricted to any sub-sample with
d if / in.
d
d KW: unit root
d KW: structural break
d KW: Lee-Strazicich
d KW: LM test
d KW: Schmidt-Phillips
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.0
d
d The package ships an example dataset, lsmlm_oecd15.dta: relative per-capita
d income for 15 OECD countries, 1870-1994, built from the Maddison Project
d Database 2023 (Bolt and Van Zanden 2024), which is distributed under a
d Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260722
d
d Author: Ibrahim Ongoren, Pamukkale University
d Support: email ongorenibrahim78@gmail.com
d
